      vals_array = np.array(vals_list)

      print("vals_list: ", vals_list)
      print("vals_array: ", vals_array)`/>
    <pre style = "border-radius: 0;">
vals_list: [1, 3, 2, 8]
vals_array: [1 3 2 8]
    </pre>
  </SubSubSection>

  <SubSubSection title = "Creating arrays using built-in functions" id = "creating_arrays_using_built_in_functions">
    <ul>
      <li><a target = "_blank" rel = "noopener noreferrer" href = "https://docs.scipy.org/doc/numpy-1.10.1/reference/generated/numpy.arange.html">np.arrage()<a/></li>
      <li><a target = "_blank" rel = "noopener noreferrer" href = "https://docs.scipy.org/doc/numpy-1.10.0/reference/generated/numpy.linspace.html">np.linspace()<a/></li>
      <li>How do we know how to call them?
        <ul>
          <li>See Documentation</li>
